      "Before 2017 test      7519 rows   fail rate 0.213\n",
      "After 2017           26701 rows   fail rate 0.226\n",
      "Random train         89658 rows   fail rate 0.225\n",
      "Random test          22415 rows   fail rate 0.225\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "pre = data[data['Period'] == 'Pre']\n",
    "post = data[data['Period'] == 'Post']\n",
    "\n",
    "# H2: 80% of Pre for training, 20% of Pre and all of Post for testing\n",
    "pre_train, pre_test = train_test_split(pre, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# H3 (placebo): the same, with 1 January 2017 as a fake change date inside Pre\n",
    "before = pre[pre['Placebo_Period'] == 'Before 2017']\n",
    "after = pre[pre['Placebo_Period'] == 'After 2017']\n",
    "before_train, before_test = train_test_split(before, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Reference: random 80/20 split of Pre and Post together (years mixed)\n",
    "pre_post = pd.concat([pre, post])\n",
    "random_train, random_test = train_test_split(pre_post, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, part in [('Pre train', pre_train), ('Pre test', pre_test), ('Post', post),\n",
    "                   ('Before 2017 train', before_train), ('Before 2017 test', before_test), ('After 2017', after),\n",
    "                   ('Random train', random_train), ('Random test', random_test)]:\n",
    "    print(f\"{name:18s} {len(part):7d} rows   fail rate {part['Fail'].mean():.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "81bc3534",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The training set with the highest number of rows is Random train with 89658 rows with a corresponding random test set of 22415 rows. They both share the same fail rate of 22.5%. Next, there is Pre train with 51434 rows and 21.6% fail rate, which has the same rate as Pre test that has 12859 rows. The sets Post, Before 2017 train, Before 2017 test, and After 2017 has 47780/23.7%, 30073/20.8%, 7519/21.3%, and 26701/22.6% respectively. In each experiment the model is tested **twice** (except for the random split, tested once): on unseen inspections from its **own** period (20% held out) and on the **later** period. The difference between the two results is the drop caused by moving to a later period. random_state=42 keeps the splits the same every time we run the notebook."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
