   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Choose the model settings with k-fold cross-validation (Chapter 10)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "a372fbd9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Decision tree, max_depth =  3: mean AUC = 0.641\n",
      "Decision tree, max_depth =  5: mean AUC = 0.660\n",
      "Decision tree, max_depth =  8: mean AUC = 0.650\n",
      "Decision tree, max_depth = 12: mean AUC = 0.612\n",
      "\n",
      "KNN, k =  5: mean AUC = 0.589\n",
      "KNN, k = 15: mean AUC = 0.612\n",
      "KNN, k = 25: mean AUC = 0.616\n",
      "KNN, k = 51: mean AUC = 0.605\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def cv_auc(model, X, y, n_splits=5):\n",
    "    kf = KFold(n_splits=n_splits, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "    scores = []\n",
    "    for train_index, val_index in kf.split(X):\n",
    "        scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "        X_tr = scaler.fit_transform(X.iloc[train_index])\n",
    "        X_val = scaler.transform(X.iloc[val_index])\n",
    "        model.fit(X_tr, y.iloc[train_index])\n",
    "        prob = model.predict_proba(X_val)[:, 1]\n",
    "        scores.append(roc_auc_score(y.iloc[val_index], prob))\n",
    "    return np.mean(scores)\n",
    "\n",
    "# a sample of 10,000 Pre training rows: KNN is slow, because every prediction compares with all training rows\n",
    "sample = pre_train.sample(10000, random_state=42)\n",
    "X_s, y_s = sample[features], sample['Fail']\n",
    "\n",
    "for depth in [3, 5, 8, 12]:\n",
    "    print(f'Decision tree, max_depth = {depth:2d}: mean AUC = {cv_auc(DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=depth, random_state=42), X_s, y_s):.3f}')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "for k in [5, 15, 25, 51]:\n",
    "    print(f'KNN, k = {k:2d}: mean AUC = {cv_auc(KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=k), X_s, y_s):.3f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "69615035",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "5-fold cross-validation **inside the Pre training data only** (the test sets are not used). A tree that is too deep and a KNN with a very small k overfit (Chapter 10); a very shallow tree or a very large k underfit. We pick the value with the highest mean AUC. We use a sample of 10,000 rows because KNN is slow (Chapter 12: \"predictions can take a long time\"); k is odd so there are no ties in the vote. The max tree depth with the highest mean AUC is 5 (mean AUC = 0.660) and the k value with the highest mean AUC is 25 (mean AUC = 0.616). `best_depth` = 5 and `best_k` = 25."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "2b86952f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "best_depth = 5   # change to the best max_depth above\n",
    "best_k = 25      # change to the best k above"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e2514cff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Both settings are at the top of their curve: the AUC first goes up (a too simple model **underfits**) and then goes down again (a too complex model **overfits**: a deep tree or a KNN with few neighbours learns the noise of the training data, Chapter 10). So we use **max_depth = 5** and **k = 25**."
   ]
  },
  {
