   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "624f2efc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The weights of the logistic regression (scaled features, so they can be compared with each other). A positive weight means the feature goes together with failing, a negative weight with passing (Chapter 12). Be careful: the features are often correlated (for example Prev_Fail and Past_Fail_Rate), so we should not read too much into one single weight. **Result:** the strongest weight by far is **Is_Reinspection (−1.142)**: a re-inspection rarely fails, because the business has fixed the problems before the inspector comes back. Inspections of businesses that have been in the data longer also fail less (Days_Since_First_Seen −0.197). The strongest positive weights are **Prev_Fail (+0.335)**, **Prev_Num_Violations (+0.295)**, **License inspections (+0.232)**, Past_Serious_Rate (+0.191), Num_Past_Inspections (+0.172) and three Zip groups (60623, 60608, 60607: +0.13 to +0.15), so the location helps too. The model relies mostly on the **history of the business**."
